course: dictionary
lesson: 14360
title: Ooh! Small words with big feelings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Ooh is a small word that shows a feeling fast. It is called an interjection, which means a word that pops out on its own to show how someone feels. «Ooh, look at those fireworks!» The word ooh tells you the speaker is surprised and delighted.
explain: The same word can show different feelings. «Ooh, that hurts!» shows pain. «Ooh, be careful, that edge looks dangerous!» shows worry. To find out which feeling it is, read the words after it and think about what is happening.
explain: When a crowd sees something amazing, people say oohs and aahs together. «Oohs and aahs filled the park as the rocket burst into gold.» Here ooh means sounds of wonder from many people at once.
fact: Ooh is an interjection, a word that shows a feeling quickly.
fact: «Ooh, that cake looks delicious!» shows delight and interest in one short word.
fact: Ooh can show surprise, delight, interest or admiration.
fact: Ooh can also show pain or worry, as in «Ooh, that hurts!»
fact: «Oohs and aahs» means sounds of wonder from a crowd.
exercise: «Ooh, look at those fireworks!» What is the ooh showing? | Hunger for dinner | Tiredness after a long day | Anger at the noise | *Surprise and delight
exercise: «Ooh, that hurts!» What does ooh show in this sentence? | Happiness | Sleepiness | *Pain | Boredom
exercise: Which phrase means sounds of wonder from a crowd? | Silent stares | Loud shouting | *Oohs and aahs | Quiet whispers
test: Which word is the interjection in «Ooh, that cake looks delicious!»? | Looks | Delicious | *Ooh | Cake
test: «Ooh, I would love to try that!» What feeling does ooh show? | *Interest and eagerness | Sleepiness | Confusion | Anger
exam: Which sentence uses ooh to show surprise? | *«Ooh, a shooting star!» | The dog sat down quietly. | Please close the door. | Two plus two is four.
